& [JustificationIdentity] is Phase3B formation reasoning
  + [justification_uuid] is 9c670f4e-cfa4-4d1f-a601-1a9c6e794b00
  + [status] is formation_justified_and_activation_rejected

& [Need] is cross from observed inference to contained candidate production
  + [reason] is Phase 2 proves a live read-only turn and Phase3A proves the exact disposable target, but neither permits a model to create a candidate implementation
  + [minimum_effect] is local mutation in only the disposable candidate worktree
  + [separation] is mutation evidence must precede authoritative sealing and independent review

& [SelectedInterface] is stable App Server workspaceWrite
  + [benefit] is exact thread, turn, sandbox, event, interrupt, and completion identities over the already proven process transport
  + [policy] is no network, no extra writable roots, excluded temp directories, approval never, one ephemeral turn
  + [Cantor] remains the existing stable read-only MCP tool
  + [reuse] is Phase 2 transport strictness and Phase3A target identity

& [HonestyDecision] is the central design constraint
  + [sandbox] may prevent physical escape only after target-host proof
  + [events] can detect and account behavior but may arrive after effects begin
  + [path_policy] is authoritative only over the later sealed filesystem state
  + [interrupt] stops continuation but is not rollback
  + [dirty_failure] is quarantined, not cleaned or retried

& [AlternativeAssessment] is explicit
  + [danger_full_access] is rejected as unnecessary and too broad
  + [direct_shell_or_command_exec] is rejected because it bypasses the intended turn boundary and may be unsandboxed
  + [model_self_report] is rejected as state proof
  + [event_only_allowlist] is rejected as preventive enforcement
  + [automatic_reset_or_worktree_delete] is deferred because cleanup is another destructive authority
  + [commit_inside_candidate] is rejected because Git history belongs to later EffectBroker authority
  + [custom_OS_sandbox] remains a possible later layer if stable workspaceWrite cannot pass the physical matrix

& [Decision] is form BCM-001 through BCM-016 but do not activate
  + [implementation] is blocked
  + [live_write] is blocked
  + [renewal] requires physical sandbox proof, mutable protocol fixtures, Phase3C sealer formation, supervisor-test rules, and a new satisfaction signature
  + [rollback] is no runtime change exists under this formation
